# M2: cold-start cost of the ingest Lambda, from its own REPORT lines.
#
# Run in CloudWatch > Logs Insights, log group /aws/lambda/noise-ingest-dev,
# time range covering the M1 run (and anything since the stack deployed).
# Read-only: it queries logs and changes nothing.
#
# Lambda writes one REPORT line per invocation. An "Init Duration" field is
# present only when that invocation had to create a new execution
# environment, which is the definition of a cold start, so this separates
# cold from warm on the provider's own measurement rather than on guesses
# from client latency.
#
# Note @duration excludes init time, so a cold invocation's total server-side
# time is @initDuration + @duration (computed as totalMs below).

filter @type = "REPORT"
| fields ispresent(@initDuration) as cold,
         @initDuration + @duration as totalMs
| stats count(*) as invocations,
        avg(@initDuration) as avgInitMs,
        pct(@initDuration, 50) as p50InitMs,
        pct(@initDuration, 95) as p95InitMs,
        max(@initDuration) as maxInitMs,
        avg(@duration) as avgHandlerMs,
        pct(@duration, 95) as p95HandlerMs,
        avg(@maxMemoryUsed / 1000 / 1000) as avgMemMB
  by cold
